IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `rra-types`

-- Renters' Rights Act 2025 (UK) — GOALS 1 AND 2: PERIODIC TENANCIES, RENT
-- PERIODS AND RENT IN ADVANCE (HA 1988 ss 4A, 4B as inserted; TFA 2019 Sch 1
-- para 1(1A)).
-- Source: ../registers/source-bundle/ukpga-2025-26.txt.

§ `Goal 1 — periodic tenancies and rent periods`

-- s 4A(1) "Terms of an assured tenancy are of no effect so far as they
-- provide— (a) for a tenancy to be a fixed term tenancy, or (b) for periods
-- of the tenancy to be different from the periods for which rent is payable".
-- (2): it has effect as a periodic tenancy with periods equal to the rent
-- periods.
@ref HA 1988 s 4A(1)-(2)
@export Whether terms of an assured tenancy are of no effect under s 4A(1) of the Housing Act 1988 as inserted by the Renters' Rights Act 2025 (UK), so that it runs as a periodic tenancy whose periods are the rent periods: terms providing for a fixed term, or for tenancy periods different from the rent periods. DRAFT, not reviewed by a UK lawyer.
GIVEN t IS A `Tenancy terms`  @desc Whether the tenancy is assured, and its fixed-term and period terms
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `fixed-term or period terms are of no effect in` t IF
        t's `an assured tenancy`
    AND (t's `provides for a fixed term` OR t's `periods of the tenancy differ from the rent periods`)

-- s 4A(3) "Terms ... which provide for the rent periods are of no effect
-- unless each rent period is— (a) a period of 28 days or shorter, or (b) a
-- monthly rent period." (5): otherwise "successive rent periods of one month
-- beginning with the first day of the tenancy".
@ref HA 1988 s 4A(3), (5), (8)
@export Whether the rent periods of an assured tenancy are permitted under s 4A(3) of the Housing Act 1988 as inserted by the Renters' Rights Act 2025 (UK): each is 28 days or shorter, or monthly; otherwise the tenancy has successive monthly rent periods from its first day (s 4A(5)). DRAFT, not reviewed by a UK lawyer.
GIVEN t IS A `Tenancy terms`  @desc The rent periods the terms provide for
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the rent periods are permitted in` t IF
    CONSIDER t's `rent periods`
    WHEN `periods of days` n THEN n AT MOST 28
    WHEN `monthly` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `longer periods, such as quarterly or yearly` THEN FALSE

§ `Goal 2 — rent in advance`

-- s 4B(12): "initial rent" is rent for the first rent period, or a later one
-- that ends during the 28 days beginning with the first day of the first
-- rent period.
@ref HA 1988 s 4B(12)
GIVEN t IS A `Tenancy terms`, r IS A `Rent period`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the rent is initial rent for` t `in` r IF
        r's `period begins on` EQUALS t's `first day of the tenancy`
    OR  r's `period ends on` AT MOST Date (Day (t's `first day of the tenancy`) PLUS 27)

-- s 4B(12) "permitted pre-tenancy period" begins when the tenancy is entered
-- into and ends with the day before its first day.
@ref HA 1988 s 4B(12)
GIVEN d IS A DATE, t IS A `Tenancy terms`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the day` d `is in the permitted pre-tenancy period of` t IF
        d AT LEAST t's `entered into on`
    AND d LESS THAN t's `first day of the tenancy`

-- s 4B(1) "Terms of an assured tenancy which provide for when rent is due are
-- of no effect so far as they provide for rent to be due in advance." (2):
-- not for a tenancy entered into before the commencement date, an excepted
-- tenancy, or initial rent due in the permitted pre-tenancy period. (12):
-- "due in advance" means due before the rent period for which it is payable.
@ref HA 1988 s 4B(1)-(2), (12)
@export Whether the term making rent for a rent period due on a given day is of no effect under s 4B of the Housing Act 1988 as inserted by the Renters' Rights Act 2025 (UK): the tenancy is assured, entered into on or after the commencement date and not excepted, and the rent is due before the rent period begins, unless it is initial rent due in the permitted pre-tenancy period. DRAFT, not reviewed by a UK lawyer.
GIVEN t IS A `Tenancy terms`  @desc The tenancy: assured, excepted, before commencement, entered into, first day
      r IS A `Rent period`    @desc The rent period and its due date under the terms
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the term for rent due in advance is of no effect for` t `in` r IF
        t's `an assured tenancy`
    AND NOT (t's `entered into before the commencement date`)
    AND NOT (t's `an excepted tenancy`)
    AND r's `due under the terms on` LESS THAN r's `period begins on`
    AND NOT (   `the rent is initial rent for` t `in` r
             AND `the day` (r's `due under the terms on`) `is in the permitted pre-tenancy period of` t)

-- s 4B(3)-(5): where the term is of no effect, the rent is due on the
-- substitute rent day: the regular rent day falling in the period if the
-- compliant rent periods have a regular pattern, otherwise the first day of
-- the rent period.
@ref HA 1988 s 4B(3)-(7)
@export The day the rent for a rent period is due under s 4B of the Housing Act 1988 as inserted by the Renters' Rights Act 2025 (UK): the day under the terms, unless that term is of no effect for rent due in advance, in which case the substitute rent day — the regular rent day in the period where the compliant periods have a regular pattern, otherwise the first day of the period. DRAFT, not reviewed by a UK lawyer.
GIVEN t IS A `Tenancy terms`  @desc The tenancy
      r IS A `Rent period`    @desc The rent period, its due date under the terms, and any regular rent day in it
GIVETH A DATE
`the day the rent is due for` t `in` r MEANS
    IF   `the term for rent due in advance is of no effect for` t `in` r
    THEN CONSIDER r's `regular rent day in this period`
         WHEN JUST d  THEN d
         WHEN NOTHING THEN r's `period begins on`
    ELSE r's `due under the terms on`

-- TFA 2019 Sch 1 para 1(1A) "a payment of rent is a prohibited payment if—
-- (a) it is payable before the tenancy is entered into, and (b) the tenancy
-- is an assured tenancy."
@ref TFA 2019 Sch 1 para 1(1A)
@export Whether a payment of rent is a prohibited payment under Schedule 1 para 1(1A) to the Tenant Fees Act 2019 as inserted by the Renters' Rights Act 2025 (UK): it is payable before the tenancy is entered into, and the tenancy is an assured tenancy. DRAFT, not reviewed by a UK lawyer.
GIVEN d IS A DATE             @desc The day the rent is payable
      t IS A `Tenancy terms`  @desc Whether the tenancy is assured, and the day it is entered into
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a payment of rent on` d `is prohibited for` t IF
        t's `an assured tenancy`
    AND d LESS THAN t's `entered into on`
